<title>ITALY: Rinascente makes 780 bln lire capital rise.</title>
<headline>Rinascente makes 780 bln lire capital rise.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian retailing group Rinascente said on Tuesday it was launching a 780 billion lire capital increase in shares, bonds and warrants.</p>
<p>A group statement said that it was to buy the Italian interests of French retail group Auchan, which include commercial centres, retail estate and service operations for 530 billion lire.</p>
<p>This news came after a complex move announced earlier to form a joint grouping between Agnelli family holding IFIL, which at present controls Rinascente, and Auchan.  </p>
<p>Auchan's interests in Italy include four hypermarkets with 2,000 employees which are expected to have 900 billion lire of sales in 1997 after some 800 billion lire in 1996.</p>
<p>Rinascente expects to have sales of around eight trillion lire in 1997 including Auchan's Italian interests.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
